-history head, via --allow-unrelated-histories'","Plan: 'There is no _carries_ticket_events gate ... the doctor instead distinguishes union from refuse purely by whether git can auto-resolve the merge.'","sync.py _do_reconverge REFUSES the unrelated-history + local-carries-events case precisely to avoid grafting an orphan store into the shared tickets branch ('Silently union-merging that would graft an orphan store into the SHARED tickets branch for everyone, which is unreviewable after the fact').","The fold folds heads INTO HEAD (the local clone's own state), not head-into-head; the same-ref argument covers the bundle heads but not the local HEAD used as the merge base."],"finding":"The doctor's 'always union' policy is justified for bundle-head-vs-bundle-head (all tips of the same configured ref), but the fold's BASE is the local HEAD whose provenance is not established; an independently-built local store (re-init / restored backup / wrong sync.remote) unrelated to the published bundles would be silently unioned via --allow-unrelated-histories into the shared ref — the exact orphan-graft outcome sync's _do_reconverge deliberately REFUSES via its _carries_ticket_events gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faa9de352e6333708","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 ('Fold the N heads by ITERATED 2-parent merges') / Scope s3_doctor.py","norm_id":"n111cc6983150976e","priority":0.3723,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A clone whose local tickets store was rebuilt independently (re-init / restored backup / wrong sync.remote) hits the multi-bundle heal path; local HEAD shares no merge-base with any published bundle head, so the first fold merges an unrelated local store into the shared ref and republishes it as T for the whole fleet."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Before folding, seed the fold from the earliest common bundle head (or an empty/unborn HEAD) rather than the arbitrary local HEAD, OR reuse _do_reconverge's _carries_ticket_events refuse gate specifically for the local-HEAD-unrelated-to-all-bundle-heads case so an independently-built local store surfaces DIVERGED/fsck-recover instead of being unioned into the shared ref.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan's contended-lock recovery narrative is internally inconsistent: it says a doctor that finds the S3 lock held should 'back off and let the normal retry re-detect', but it also specifies a single `healed_once` guard that trips on ANY heal invocation -- including a no-op return when the lock was unavailable. A doctor that loses the S3 lock therefore consumes its one heal attempt without collapsing the bundles; the retried push still hits the multi-bundle state, `healed_once` blocks re-invocation, and the push falls through to the non-FF/terminal classification instead of re-healing. The loser of a repair storm never converges on that push (it must wait for a whole new push cycle).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff42838866fc93309","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Heal algorithm step 1 (lock back-off) vs. Detection paragraph (`healed_once` guard)","norm_id":"n84bc7722f65adbbb","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Have `heal_multi_bundle` distinguish 'locked/no-op' from 'healed' in its return, and in `push_tickets_branch` set `healed_once=True` only on an effective heal; for a 'locked' outcome, apply a bounded backoff-and-re-detect (small attempt cap) so the loser re-enters detection after the winner converges.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Strengthen the API-surface contract test to pin BEHAVIOR, not just symbol names: assert S3Remote's constructor accepts the positional (scheme, profile, bucket, prefix) arity, that acquire_lock's contention path returns None (not raises) and success returns a lock key, and that get_bundles_for_ref returns the element shape _sha_from_key parses — and classify the v0.3.2 surface evidence as Partially-verified (source-inspected, not importable in CI) so Pass-2 weighs the private-API risk.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["resolve_symbol('git_remote_s3','S3Remote') -> UNRESOLVED (not importable in this environment)","Plan: 'acquire_lock(ref) (its IfNoneMatch=\"*\" conditional-put, 60s TTL, stale-lock steal, remote.py); on None/412 another repair is in flight'","Plan Testing: 'A contract test ... asserts the exact v0.3.2 surface ... so a helper upgrade that moves or renames any of them fails loudly here' — as implemented in-repo the check is hasattr(S3Remote, attr) (name-level), which does not pin the positional constructor arity or the lock return contract","Plan Scope: 'All git_remote_s3 access is routed through a single thin adapter function ... so the private-API dependency has one swappable seam' (mitigation present)"],"finding":"The plan binds to git_remote_s3's private API by BEHAVIOR (positional constructor S3Remote(scheme,profile,bucket,prefix); acquire_lock returning a key / None / 412; get_bundles_for_ref return shape; IfNoneMatch=* 60s-TTL lock), but the drift guard it ships is described as a name-level contract test (import + attribute existence). Names can survive a signature/return-contract change, so the guard would not 'fail loudly here rather than at runtime' for the bindings that actually matter. The library is not importable in this environment, so the asserted 'verified against v0.3.2' surface is Unverified here and Partially-verified at best from the plan's cited source inspection.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f162ab32414918bff","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 & Heal algorithm; Scope (single-adapter seam); Testing (credential-less API-surface guard)","norm_id":"n0ee5c2df2e07a9b3","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["git-remote-s3 releases a minor version that keeps symbol names